  "description": "FlowMediator is an opinionated mediator library for explicit application flow in .NET 8 and .NET 9.\n\n      It provides clear separation between request-based application flow (SendAsync)\n      and event-based side effects (PublishAsync), with pipeline support for CQRS-style\n      applications and explicit event handling.",
  "id": "FlowMediator",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-01-26T19:02:19.107Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "ndZG2QcpkqoTpxQFY+5NWG3aJEH2fPtd9yf50fxX6rQFv+Is5DIZnWbakJtVltNGGWXsb1965VJ6XNBbPEodZA==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 36323,
  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/berk2k/FlowMediator",
  "published": "2026-01-26T18:59:44.447Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.NUGET.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v2.0.1\n    - Docs: clarified PublishAsync semantics (in-process, sequential; order not guaranteed unless controlled)\n    - Docs: clarified exception behavior (stop and rethrow on handler exception)\n\n    v2.0.0\n    - Explicit separation between Send (application flow) and Publish (events)\n    - Events are no longer treated as requests\n    - Multiple event handlers supported\n    - Pipeline applies only to SendAsync\n    - Event handlers are executed sequentially (in-process) by default\n    - Breaking change: migration from v1.x is required",
  "repository": "",
